abstract: >
  FloodWatch.PH is an open-source two-track system for measuring observed flood
  extent and flood recurrence from public satellite data over the Philippines.
  Track A applies classical Sentinel-1 SAR Otsu change detection to produce
  per-timestep flood-extent GeoJSON for real typhoon events, validated against the
  Global Flood Database. Track B trains a logistic-regression head on frozen Google
  AlphaEarth Satellite Embedding V1 (64-dim, CC-BY-4.0) with Platt-sigmoid
  calibration on an event-disjoint holdout to classify per-pixel flood recurrence
  proneness. The build is bit-exact reproducible from a committed 10 MB embeddings
  cache with no GPU required.
